From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flax <flax@tiogapass>
Date: Thu, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] make BMC reset audit event meaningful

A Redfish BMC GracefulRestart/ForceRestart logs an audit event via
alertSystem("Alert:" + resetType).  bmcweb's fillEventLogEntryJson builds
the Redfish MessageId as "OpenBMC.0.5.0." + Message.substr(0, firstColon),
so "Alert:GracefulRestart" collapses to the useless "OpenBMC.0.5.0.Alert"
and the reset type (the only interesting part) is discarded.

Move the meaningful token before the colon: "BMC" + resetType yields
"OpenBMC.0.5.0.BMCGracefulRestart" / "OpenBMC.0.5.0.BMCForceRestart".
The event stays Informational (Redfish "OK") - we want BMC reboots
recorded for audit, just not flagged as a problem.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [single-platform policy]
---
 redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp b/redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp
+++ b/redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp
@@ -231,7 +231,7 @@ inline void resetOperation(const std::shared_ptr<bmcweb::AsyncResp>& asyncResp,
 {
     if (resetType == "GracefulRestart")
     {
-        std::string alertMessageId = "Alert:" + resetType;
+        std::string alertMessageId = "BMC" + resetType;
         EventServiceManager::getInstance().alertSystem(alertMessageId);
         BMCWEB_LOG_ERROR("Proceeding with", resetType);
         doBMCGracefulRestart(asyncResp);
@@ -239,7 +239,7 @@ inline void resetOperation(const std::shared_ptr<bmcweb::AsyncResp>& asyncResp,
     }
     if (resetType == "ForceRestart")
     {
-        std::string alertMessageId = "Alert:" + resetType;
+        std::string alertMessageId = "BMC" + resetType;
         EventServiceManager::getInstance().alertSystem(alertMessageId);
         BMCWEB_LOG_ERROR("Proceeding with", resetType);
         doBMCForceRestart(asyncResp);
